+| EX4 | Arch builds pacman with `-Dscriptlet-shell=/usr/bin/bash`, so every install, upgrade and removal scriptlet that libalpm runs starts as `/usr/bin/bash -c '. <scriptlet>; <function> <version> [<old version>]'` through `_alpm_run_chroot`; the path is fixed at build time by the packaging and the `.INSTALL` file is sourced, so a shebang in it stays inert; `<version>` is the caller's `ver`: the new full version for `pre_install`/`post_install`, new then old for `pre_upgrade`/`post_upgrade`, the removed package's version for `pre_remove`/`post_remove` (TO4, TO7; PKGBUILD(5) 520-549); the upstream build default is `/bin/sh` (S219 meson_options.txt:17), which this root links to bash, so the flag selects POSIX mode (making the `BASH_ENV` removal of EX3 load-bearing) rather than bash-only syntax support | `/usr/bin/bash` | S220 PKGBUILD:113-115 “-Ddoc=enabled \ -Ddoxygen=enabled \ -Dscriptlet-shell=/usr/bin/bash \” (S222 trans.c:357-358 `strcpy(arg0, SCRIPTLET_SHELL)`, `"-c"`; command line :400-406; run :410) | `/usr/lib/libalpm.so.16.0.1` (owned by pacman 7.1.0.r9.g54d9411-3) carries the string `/usr/bin/bash` (strings index 1277) and lacks `/bin/sh` (S225 `libalpm-shell-strings.txt`) |
